𝗥𝗲𝗰𝘂𝗿𝗿𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗲𝗱𝘂𝗹𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝘄𝗶𝘁𝗵 𝗖𝗿𝗼𝗻

If you’ve ever wanted your scripts or tasks to run automatically at fixed times (every minute, daily at midnight, every Monday, etc.), use cron.

Here’s a quick guide:

*   *   *   *   *  command_to_run
-   -   -   -   -
|   |   |   |   +----- Day of week (0–6) (Sun=0)
|   |   |   +----------- Month (1–12)
|   |   +----------------- Day of month (1–31)
|   +----------------------- Hour (0–23)
+----------------------------- Minute (0–59)


✨ 𝗖𝗼𝗺𝗺𝗼𝗻 𝗰𝗼𝗺𝗺𝗮𝗻𝗱𝘀

𝘤𝘳𝘰𝘯𝘵𝘢𝘣 -𝘭 → list all scheduled jobs

𝘤𝘳𝘰𝘯𝘵𝘢𝘣 -𝘦 → edit cron jobs

